<div id="" class="hds-featured-link-list bg-spacesuit-white padding-x-2 tablet:padding-x-3 desktop:padding-x-4 padding-y-5 desktop:padding-y-6 hds-module hds-module-full alignfull wp-block-nasa-blocks-featured-link-list">	<div class="grid-container grid-container-block padding-0">
		<div class="margin-bottom-4">
			<h2 class="heading-22">
				Learn More			</h2>
		</div>

					<div class="grid-row padding-y-2 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-30-important">
				<div class="grid-row featured-link-list-row width-full flex-align-center">
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 tablet:padding-right-3 desktop:padding-right-5">
						<div class="width-full">
							<div class="hds-cover-wrapper width-full ratio-1x1 radius-pill overflow-hidden">
								<figure class="hds-media-background "><img decoding="async" width="1546" height="1920" src="https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=1546&amp;h=1920&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail" alt="Scott Carpenter next to a NASA sign" style="transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 1% 35%; object-position: 1% 35%; object-fit: cover;" block_context="nasa-block" loading="lazy" srcset="https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=1546&amp;h=1920&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1546w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=242&amp;h=301&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 242w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=768&amp;h=954&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=825&amp;h=1025&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 825w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=1237&amp;h=1536&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1237w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=322&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 322w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=483&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 483w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=725&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 725w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/62-MA7-55/62-MA7-55~large.jpg?w=966&amp;h=1200&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 966w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1546px) 100vw, 1546px" /></figure>							</div>
						</div> 
					</div>
					<div class="grid-col-8 desktop:grid-col-10 padding-left-3 desktop:padding-left-0">
						<div class="grid-row flex-align-center">
							<div class="grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6">
								<h2 class="heading-36 margin-0">Project Mercury Overview</h2>
							</div>
							<div class="grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6">
								<p class="p-md margin-0 color-carbon-black">Initiated in 1958, completed in 1963, Project Mercury was the United States&#039; first man-in-space program. The objectives of the program, which made six manned flights from 1961 to 1963, were specific.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 display-flex flex-justify-end">
						<a href="https://www.nasa.gov/missions/project-mercury/project-mercury-overview-introduction/" target="" aria-label="Project Mercury Overview">
                            <svg class="hds-featured-link-list-button margin-left-auto margin-right-0" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none">
                                <circle class="color-nasa-red" cx="16" cy="16" r="16"></circle><path d="M8 16.956h12.604l-3.844 4.106 1.252 1.338L24 16l-5.988-6.4-1.252 1.338 3.844 4.106H8v1.912z" class="color-spacesuit-white"></path>
                            </svg>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="grid-row padding-y-2 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-30-important">
				<div class="grid-row featured-link-list-row width-full flex-align-center">
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 tablet:padding-right-3 desktop:padding-right-5">
						<div class="width-full">
							<div class="hds-cover-wrapper width-full ratio-1x1 radius-pill overflow-hidden">
								<figure class="hds-media-background "><img decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/edu_what_was_project_mercury.jpg?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;crop=1" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail" alt="Friendship 7 launches atop an Atlas rocket" style="transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;" block_context="nasa-block" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/edu_what_was_project_mercury.jpg?resize=150,150 150w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/edu_what_was_project_mercury.jpg?resize=50,50 50w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/edu_what_was_project_mercury.jpg?resize=100,100 100w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/edu_what_was_project_mercury.jpg?resize=200,200 200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></figure>							</div>
						</div> 
					</div>
					<div class="grid-col-8 desktop:grid-col-10 padding-left-3 desktop:padding-left-0">
						<div class="grid-row flex-align-center">
							<div class="grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6">
								<h2 class="heading-36 margin-0">Project Mercury Objectives and Guidelines</h2>
							</div>
							<div class="grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6">
								<p class="p-md margin-0 color-carbon-black">The objectives of the Mercury Project, as stated at the time of project go-ahead, were as follows: 1. Place a manned spacecraft in orbital flight around the earth. 2. Investigate man&#039;s performance capabilities and his ability to function in the environment of space. 3. Recover the man and the spacecraft safely.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 display-flex flex-justify-end">
						<a href="https://www.nasa.gov/missions/project-mercury/project-mercury-overview-objectives-and-guidelines/" target="" aria-label="Project Mercury Objectives and Guidelines">
                            <svg class="hds-featured-link-list-button margin-left-auto margin-right-0" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none">
                                <circle class="color-nasa-red" cx="16" cy="16" r="16"></circle><path d="M8 16.956h12.604l-3.844 4.106 1.252 1.338L24 16l-5.988-6.4-1.252 1.338 3.844 4.106H8v1.912z" class="color-spacesuit-white"></path>
                            </svg>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="grid-row padding-y-2 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-30-important">
				<div class="grid-row featured-link-list-row width-full flex-align-center">
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 tablet:padding-right-3 desktop:padding-right-5">
						<div class="width-full">
							<div class="hds-cover-wrapper width-full ratio-1x1 radius-pill overflow-hidden">
								<figure class="hds-media-background "><img decoding="async" width="1233" height="1920" src="https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=1233&amp;h=1920&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail" alt="Alan Shepard wears his silver Mercury space suit." style="transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 57% 6%; object-position: 57% 6%; object-fit: cover;" block_context="nasa-block" loading="lazy" srcset="https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=1233&amp;h=1920&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1233w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=193&amp;h=301&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 193w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=768&amp;h=1196&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=658&amp;h=1025&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 658w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=986&amp;h=1535&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 986w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=257&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 257w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=385&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 385w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=578&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 578w, https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/8772553/8772553~large.jpg?w=771&amp;h=1201&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 771w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1233px) 100vw, 1233px" /></figure>							</div>
						</div> 
					</div>
					<div class="grid-col-8 desktop:grid-col-10 padding-left-3 desktop:padding-left-0">
						<div class="grid-row flex-align-center">
							<div class="grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6">
								<h2 class="heading-36 margin-0">Project Mercury Astronaut Selection</h2>
							</div>
							<div class="grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6">
								<p class="p-md margin-0 color-carbon-black">Now that men had been chosen to serve as the focal points for all this effort, new spirits animated the Space Task Group. Indeed, the Nation as a whole began to participate vicariously in Project Mercury when, on April 9, 1959, at a press conference  the public met the seven men chosen to be this Nation’s nominees for the first human voyagers into space.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 display-flex flex-justify-end">
						<a href="https://www.nasa.gov/history/project-mercury-overview-astronaut-selection/" target="" aria-label="Project Mercury Astronaut Selection">
                            <svg class="hds-featured-link-list-button margin-left-auto margin-right-0" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none">
                                <circle class="color-nasa-red" cx="16" cy="16" r="16"></circle><path d="M8 16.956h12.604l-3.844 4.106 1.252 1.338L24 16l-5.988-6.4-1.252 1.338 3.844 4.106H8v1.912z" class="color-spacesuit-white"></path>
                            </svg>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
					<div class="grid-row padding-y-2 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-30-important">
				<div class="grid-row featured-link-list-row width-full flex-align-center">
					<div class="grid-col-2 desktop:grid-col-1 tablet:padding-right-3 desktop:padding-right-5">
						<div class="width-full">
							<div class="hds-cover-wrapper width-full ratio-1x1 radius-pill overflow-hidden">
								<figure class="hds-media-background "><img decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/freedom_7_7_glenn_grissom_shepard_w_redstone_rocket_s61-00239.jpg?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;crop=1" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail" alt="Freedom 7 crew of John Glen, Gus Grissom, and Alan Shepard in their space suits in front of the Redstone rocket." style="transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;" block_context="nasa-block" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/freedom_7_7_glenn_grissom_shepard_w_redstone_rocket_s61-00239.jpg?resize=150,150 150w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/freedom_7_7_glenn_grissom_shepard_w_redstone_rocket_s61-00239.jpg?resize=50,50 50w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/freedom_7_7_glenn_grissom_shepard_w_redstone_rocket_s61-00239.jpg?resize=100,100 100w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/freedom_7_7_glenn_grissom_shepard_w_redstone_rocket_s61-00239.jpg?resize=200,200 200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></figure>							</div>
						</div> 
